From 20adafc2400627629cb631ff99118676dea93f40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:47:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-92: the grid shown and snapping to it are two
 toolbar buttons, like WPF (0.92.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF (Create UIs > the artboard toolbar): "Show/Hide snap grid" and "Turn
on/off snapping to gridlines" are two commands. Here the toolbar's 格線 did
both. Now 格線 = drawn or not (GRID.show, htd.gridShow) and 吸附 = snapping or
not (GRID.on, htd.gridOn), apart, for every page, remembered (show never set =
as the snapping, so nothing changes for a saved state). The title bar's # and
the right-click item still turn both on / off together.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 183, panels, real VS Code 157):
probe (snapping without the grid drawn lands on multiples of 8; the grid
drawn without snapping moves freely by 5; the toolbar posts gridShow,
gridSnap); smoke (the two kept apart, every page told).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
